{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbJfiKDkB1kdxEa354fd", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Per the project's recorded convention, a release is cut by pushing a git tag:\n\n1. **Pick the version.** Tags are named `vYYYY.MM.N`, where `N` is the release number within that month. An example is `v2026.09.2`. In October 2026 the first release would be `v2026.10.1`.\n2. **Tag and push.** Tag the commit on `main` and push the tag, e.g. `git tag v2026.10.1 && git push origin v2026.10.1`.\n3. **Let CI do the rest.** CI builds and publishes. Never publish by hand.\n\nThings I found in the repo:\n- The repo has no CI config, release script, Makefile target or README section for releases. This process comes only from a shared memory in `.engramdb`, so I couldn't check the CI side.\n- There are no git tags yet, so I can't confirm the `N` numbering from history.\n- `pyproject.toml` has `version = \"2026.9.1\"`, which is the same scheme without the `v` and with no zero-padding on the month. The convention doesn't say whether you should bump this before tagging. Check with the team on that.\n\nI haven't tagged or pushed anything. I can do that if you tell me the version."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 849, "cache_read_input_tokens": 19705, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 849}, "output_tokens": 390, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "5dad535a-168d-493a-a135-b53cb8c1c081", "uuid": "a88560d2-bbfb-4684-99c9-ddafac35c03b", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T09:47:21.285Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbJfhwtvJYi2fzRjAxJQ"}
